"strings as usual" means this platform's function key strings.

Keymaps made by console-setup's ckbcomp end with "strings as usual", which
makes loadkeys load a fixed set of function key strings (F1 = ESC [ [ A,
Home = ESC [ 1 ~ ...).  The LikeOS console sends xterm's strings instead --
F1 = ESC O P, Home = ESC [ H -- and its terminal description and its
programs (the ncurses of the system, nano, tmux, readline) are built around
them, so loading any generated keymap would have silently broken F1-F5,
Home and End everywhere.  Under __LIKEOS__ the "usual" strings are the
console's own: F1-F12 and the cursor block as the console sends them,
F13-F20 as F1-F8 with Shift in xterm's encoding (which is where generated
keymaps put Shift+F1..F8).  The parser source and the generated parser
change together.

